; C2  The table's convention, not the book's (Jason, 2026-10-12). The book's
; nearest statement is Winning 42 p. 25 (W42-p025-a), and it runs the other way.
; Rule, in our words: the bidder's partner, following the bidder's trump lead
; and holding the highest trump still unplayed, plays it.
; Python gate (pour_bidder gate_c2): the same; no difference.
; The book reads that play as "it was the partner's only trump"; the table's
; sender plays it with other trumps too. The book's own Hand 30 (p. 103) has
; the partner play the top trump while holding two more: the book's play is the
; sender's, and its reading is false there. The reading is a query:
; c02-reading-singleton.silas.
(policy c02-high-trump-handoff
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule play-the-top-trump (select answer)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles (chair b) (chair p) (domino top))
        (out top)
        (pattern
          (viewer p)
          (declarer b)
          (partner b p)
          (leader b)
          (led-context q*)
          (own-legal top)
          (boss top q*))))))
